# VoiceVision Feature: Auto Language Detection (T032)
# Source: src/voicevision/backends/whisper_cpp.py, src/voicevision/server.py, src/voicevision/listen.py

## WhisperCppBackend.detect_language()
- Runs whisper.cpp with --detect-language flag
- Parses "detected language: en" or "language: en" from output
- Returns ISO 639-1 code (en, pt, es, etc.)
- Raises BackendExecutionError if detection fails

## WhisperCppBackend.transcribe(language="auto")
- If language="auto": calls detect_language() then transcribes with detected lang
- If language="pt": uses pt for this call (rebuilds argv)
- If language=None: uses constructor language

## VoiceVisionService.transcribe()
- Handles language="auto" by creating temp backend for detection
- Then transcribes with detected language
- Returns (transcript, elapsed_ms) as usual

## HTTP /transcribe
- Accepts "language": "auto" in request body
- Returns detected_language field when auto used

## WebSocket /stream
- Accepts "language": "auto" in audio frames

## CLI voicevision-listen
- --language auto enables detection